Task 3: Automate Discovery and Registration for New Systems
Subtask 3.1: Create Host Groups for Automation
Navigate to Configure → Host Groups in the Foreman interface.

Create a new host group for automated registration:

Name: auto-discovery
Parent: (none)
Environment: production
Puppet CA Proxy: foreman.example.com
Puppet Master Proxy: foreman.example.com
Configure the Operating System tab:

Architecture: x86_64
Operating System: CentOS 7
Media: CentOS mirror
Partition Table: Kickstart default
PXE Loader: PXELinux BIOS
Save the host group configuration.

Subtask 3.2: Configure Auto-Provisioning Rules
Navigate to Hosts → Provisioning Templates.

Create a custom discovery rule template:

cat > /tmp/auto-discovery-rule.erb << 'EOF'
<%#
kind: discovery
name: Auto Discovery Rule
%>

# Auto-discovery rule for new hosts
if @host.facts['discovery_bootif']
  # Set host group based on network interface
  if @host.facts['discovery_bootif'].match(/^52:54:00/)
    @host.hostgroup = Hostgroup.find_by_name('auto-discovery')
  end
  
  # Set hostname based on MAC address
  mac = @host.facts['discovery_bootif'].gsub(':', '')
  @host.name = "auto-#{mac[-6..-1]}.example.com"
  
  # Auto-provision if conditions are met
  if @host.facts['memorysize_mb'].to_i > 1024
    @host.provision!
  end
end
EOF
Upload the template to Foreman:
hammer template create \
  --name "Auto Discovery Rule" \
  --type discovery \
  --file /tmp/auto-discovery-rule.erb
Subtask 3.3: Configure Discovery Rules
In the Foreman web interface, navigate to Configure → Discovery Rules.

Create a new discovery rule:

Rule Details:
  Name: Auto Registration Rule
  Search: facts.memorysize_mb > 1024
  Host Group: auto-discovery
  Hostname: discovery-<%= @host.facts['discovery_bootif'].gsub(':', '') %>
  
Actions:
  Enabled: Yes
  Priority: 100
  Max Count: 10
Configure advanced rule conditions:
# Memory-based rule
facts.memorysize_mb > 2048 AND facts.processorcount >= 2

# Network-based rule  
facts.discovery_bootif ~ "^52:54:00"

# Combined rule
facts.memorysize_mb > 1024 AND facts.discovery_bootif ~ "^52:54:00" AND facts.is_virtual = true
Save the discovery rule.
Subtask 3.4: Test Automated Discovery
Create or start a new virtual machine that meets the rule criteria.

Boot the new system from the discovery ISO.

Monitor the discovery process in the Foreman logs:

tail -f /var/log/foreman/production.log | grep -i discovery
Verify that the system is automatically discovered and provisioned:
# Check discovered hosts
hammer discovery list

# Check managed hosts
hammer host list --search "name ~ discovery"
Subtask 3.5: Create Bulk Registration Script
Create a script for bulk host registration:
cat > /tmp/bulk-register.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

# Bulk registration script for discovered hosts
FOREMAN_URL="https://foreman.example.com"
USERNAME="admin"
PASSWORD="admin123"

# Get list of discovered hosts
DISCOVERED_HOSTS=$(hammer --username $USERNAME --password $PASSWORD discovery list --output csv | tail -n +2)

while IFS=',' read -r id name mac ip subnet; do
    echo "Processing discovered host: $name ($mac)"
    
    # Auto-provision based on criteria
    MEMORY=$(hammer --username $USERNAME --password $PASSWORD discovery info --id $id --output yaml | grep memorysize_mb | awk '{print $2}')
    
    if [ "$MEMORY" -gt 2048 ]; then
        echo "Auto-provisioning host $name with sufficient memory ($MEMORY MB)"
        
        hammer --username $USERNAME --password $PASSWORD discovery provision \
            --id $id \
            --hostgroup "auto-discovery" \
            --name "auto-$mac" \
            --domain "example.com" \
            --subnet "default"
            
        echo "Host $name provisioned successfully"
    else
        echo "Host $name does not meet memory requirements ($MEMORY MB)"
    fi
    
done <<< "$DISCOVERED_HOSTS"
EOF
Make the script executable and run it:
chmod +x /tmp/bulk-register.sh
/tmp/bulk-register.sh
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Discovery ISO Not Booting
Problem: System fails to boot from discovery ISO

Solution:

# Verify ISO integrity
md5sum /tmp/foreman-discovery.iso

# Check ISO contents
mount -o loop /tmp/foreman-discovery.iso /mnt
ls -la /mnt/

# Recreate ISO with proper parameters
genisoimage -o /tmp/foreman-discovery-fixed.iso \
  -b isolinux/isolinux.bin \
  -c isolinux/boot.cat \
  -no-emul-boot \
  -boot-load-size 4 \
  -boot-info-table \
  -V "FDIROOT" \
  /var/lib/tftpboot/boot/fdi-image/
Issue 2: Host Not Appearing in Discovery
Problem: Booted host doesn't appear in discovered hosts list

Solution:

# Check Foreman proxy logs
tail -f /var/log/foreman-proxy/proxy.log

# Verify discovery plugin status
foreman-rake plugin:list | grep discovery

# Check network connectivity from discovered host
# (from discovery environment console)
ping foreman.example.com
curl -k https://foreman.example.com
Issue 3: Auto-Provisioning Fails
Problem: Discovery rules don't trigger automatic provisioning

Solution:

# Check discovery rule syntax
hammer discovery-rule list

# Verify host group configuration
hammer hostgroup info --name "auto-discovery"

# Test rule matching manually
hammer discovery provision --id <discovery_id> --hostgroup "auto-discovery"

# Check provisioning logs
tail -f /var/log/foreman/production.log | grep -i provision
